5,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I’m worried about the depot floor. Freight doesn’t pause for office projects. We need a system that survives our actual yards and calendar.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Kenji, the floor is critical, but I’m watching the long-term bill. We need to know what this system truly costs us after the initial approval.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the floor matters, but I’m watching for the same old failure: unclear ownership when things break, and plans that drift from reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Rin,,"I keep seeing two bad patterns: systems that just get old, and outside help that leaves a mess. We have to avoid both!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,"I hear your worries. But remember, the people who run these systems are our true foundation. We must ensure the change supports them, not just the machines.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, you’re right about the people. But if the yard scanners crash during peak season, no amount of support saves the freight. We need hardware that fits our actual mix.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, hardware is vital, but I worry about the recurring costs. We must ensure the long-term bill doesn’t surprise us after the initial approval.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, recurring costs are a symptom. The root is unclear ownership. If no one is in charge when it breaks, the bill just grows.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, ownership is key! But I also worry about systems that quietly age. We need something that stays fresh, not just someone to blame when it breaks!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right. A system that ages quietly is a burden on the people who must maintain it. We must choose a path that respects their energy and skill.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree. If the system ages, the yard suffers. We need something that keeps up with our daily chaos, not just a pretty dashboard.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, aging systems are a trap. But I’m focused on the hidden costs. We need to see the full lifecycle bill, not just the sticker price.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I agree. But cost is a symptom of poor ownership. If no one is accountable for the system, the bill grows. We need clear responsibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I hear you! But if the system gets old, nobody wants to own it. We need something that stays useful, not just a clear blame line!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, clarity is good, but people are the heart. We must ensure the new system does not stretch our remaining staff too thin.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree. But we also need to check the yard devices. If the new system doesn’t fit our old scanners, the floor stops. Let’s look into that.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the yard devices are vital, but I need to see the renewal invoices. I want to know if the long-term bill is hidden in the fine print.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I need to see who owned support during last winter’s outage. That tells me if we are walking into the same ownership gap again.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I’ll check the dispatch tool’s upgrade history! If we keep skipping updates, it just gets older and harder to fix.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the yard devices are vital. I will look into the administrator retirements to see how thin our people are.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
