36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the yard chaos is real, but look at my findings. Capital gets cut, yet operating costs pass easily. We are trapped in a cycle of hidden, recurring bills.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, your cost cycle is real, but my findings show the root cause. Support is scattered across four suppliers, and last winter’s outage sat unowned for two days.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that sounds scary! But I found our dispatch tool skipped three upgrades since 2012. It’s just getting older and harder to fix!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, that aging system burdens our people. I found two key admins retire this year, and hiring took eleven months. We are dangerously thin on skilled hands.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, skipping upgrades is exactly why we’re stuck. @Servas, losing two admins now is terrifying. We need a system that doesn’t rely on heroes to survive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, your ownership gap explains the cost creep. @Servas, with admins retiring, we must avoid a model that demands constant expert intervention.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
